"There are four seasons in Viet Nam. In spring, it is warm and sometimes rainy. I usually wear a blouse and jeans. In summer, it is very hot, so I wear a T-shirt and shorts. In autumn, it is cool and I wear trousers and a light jumper. In winter, it is cold in the North. I wear a thick jumper and a coat.":"data:audio/mpeg;base64,",
"Viet Nam has four seasons in the North. Spring starts in February. It is warm, and flowers bloom everywhere. In summer, it is very hot and sometimes stormy, so people usually wear T-shirts and shorts. Autumn is the most comfortable season. It is cool and sunny, and many students wear jumpers in the morning. Winter is the coldest season. People wear coats, scarves and warm trousers. In the South, however, it is hot all year round, and there are only two seasons: the rainy season and the dry season.":"data:audio/mpeg;base64,",
"My favourite season is autumn. In autumn, the weather in Ha Noi is cool and sunny. I usually wear jeans and a light jumper. The leaves are yellow and beautiful. I like walking in the park and flying kites with my friends. Autumn is the most beautiful season of the year.":"data:audio/mpeg;base64,",
